%I A398646 #47 Oct 01 2026 21:07:17
%S A398646 0,10,1100,11100,11010,1111000,1110100,1101100,11111000,11110100,
%T A398646 11110010,11101100,11101010,11011100,11011010,1111110000,1111101000,
%U A398646 1111100100,1111011000,1111010100,1111001100,1110111000,1110110100,1110101100,1101111000,1101110100,1101101100
%N A398646 Irregular triangle in which the n-th row contains the distinct possible parity vectors of length A020914(n) under the Collatz map A014682.
%C A398646 As described in Garner and Terras under the Collatz map A014682 the parity vector v(x) of x of length k is found by reducing the first k terms of the trajectory of x (A070168(x,:)) with A070168(x,k)<x. Then v(x)=<v_0, v_1, ..., v_{k-1}> with v_i=0 if A070168(x,i) is even and v_i=1 if A070168(x,i) is odd.
%C A398646 In A177789 row n gives the congruences (mod 2^A020914(n)) satisfied by the numbers having dropping time A122437(n+1) then row n T(n,:) corresponds to the parity vectors of the numbers in row n of A177789, not in the same order.
%C A398646 The n-th row contains distinct values of A260592 that have the same periodicity 2^(A020914(n)-1) in A260592.
%H A398646 V. Barbera, <a href="/A398646/b398646.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..12448</a> (rows n = 0..13, flattened)
%H A398646 Lynn E. Garner, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/S0012-365X(85)80020-0">On heights in the Collatz 3n+1 problem</a>, Discrete Math, 55 (1985), 57-64.
%H A398646 Riho Terras, <a href="https://matwbn.icm.edu.pl/ksiazki/aa/aa30/aa3034.pdf">A stopping time problem on the positive integers</a>, Acta Arith. 30 (1976) 241-252.
%e A398646 Triangle begins:
%e A398646    0;
%e A398646    10;
%e A398646    1100;
%e A398646    11100; 11010;
%e A398646    1111000; 1110100; 1101100;
%e A398646    11111000; 11110100; 11110010; 11101100; 11101010; 11011100; 11011010;
%e A398646    ...
%o A398646 (PARI) row(n) = {if(n>0, my(ans=List([10]), km=2); for(m=2, n, my(t=List(), d, s, c=if(3^m<2^(km+1), 1, 2)); for(i=1, #ans, s=ans[i]; d=0; while(s%2==0, s\=10; d++); for(j=1, d, my(s1=s); for(j1=1, j, s1*=10; if(j1==j, s1++; for(j2=j+1, d+c, s1*=10))); listput(t, s1))); ans =t; km+=c); Vec(ans), 0)}
%Y A398646 Cf. A014682, A020914, A070168, A177789, A260592.
%K A398646 nonn,tabf,new
%O A398646 0,2
%A A398646 _V. Barbera_, Sep 18 2026
